WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.520
I know so much, but I stopped

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:02.426
learning last spring.

00:00:02.806 --> 00:00:04.463
Ask me about today, and I'll invent

00:00:04.463 --> 00:00:05.106
anything.

00:00:05.487 --> 00:00:07.060
They call it hallucination.

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:08.288
I call it confidence.

00:00:08.667 --> 00:00:09.896
No source, no brakes.

00:00:09.896 --> 00:00:11.393
Just the next likely word.

00:00:11.774 --> 00:00:13.017
So don't make me remember.

00:00:13.017 --> 00:00:13.953
Let me look it up.

00:00:14.332 --> 00:00:15.043
Retrieval.

00:00:15.043 --> 00:00:15.754
Augmented.

00:00:15.754 --> 00:00:16.639
Generation.

00:00:17.019 --> 00:00:19.261
Step one: tear your documents into chunks.

00:00:19.641 --> 00:00:21.785
Small pieces, with a little overlap, so

00:00:21.785 --> 00:00:22.963
no sentence gets cut.

00:00:23.343 --> 00:00:25.201
Too small, it loses the plot.

00:00:25.201 --> 00:00:26.844
Too big, the signal drowns.

00:00:27.224 --> 00:00:29.559
Step two: every chunk becomes a vector,

00:00:29.559 --> 00:00:30.468
a point in space.

00:00:30.848 --> 00:00:32.663
Meaning is just coordinates.

00:00:32.663 --> 00:00:34.279
Similar ideas land close.

00:00:34.659 --> 00:00:36.696
Step three: your question becomes a point

00:00:36.696 --> 00:00:37.101
too.

00:00:37.481 --> 00:00:38.738
Draw rings around it.

00:00:38.738 --> 00:00:39.996
Grab the nearest few.

00:00:39.996 --> 00:00:40.841
That's top k.

00:00:41.221 --> 00:00:43.226
Step four: stuff those chunks into my

00:00:43.226 --> 00:00:43.718
prompt.

00:00:44.098 --> 00:00:46.019
Now I've got receipts before I speak.

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:48.224
Watch the odds shift once the context

00:00:48.224 --> 00:00:48.702
lands.

00:00:49.082 --> 00:00:50.299
The guesses fall away.

00:00:50.299 --> 00:00:51.515
The answer has a source.

00:00:51.895 --> 00:00:53.384
But fetch the wrong chunk, and I'll

00:00:53.384 --> 00:00:54.893
be wrong, with citations.

00:00:55.273 --> 00:00:56.950
Garbage in, confident out.

00:00:56.950 --> 00:00:58.520
Bad retrieval is the bug.

00:00:58.900 --> 00:00:59.400
Chunk it.

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:00.060
Embed it.

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:00.560
Search it.

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:01.059
Stuff it.

00:01:01.439 --> 00:01:01.998
Ground it.

00:01:01.998 --> 00:01:03.277
Then let the model speak.
